  "details": "- CVE-2026-53793: widen the daemon path-confinement gate to cover a chrooted\n  module whose path carries a \"/./\" inner boundary marker, and route the\n  resolver trust root and do_mkdir_at through the same predicate\n- CVE-2026-53796: confine the non-daemon receiver's destination chdir,\n  refusing a destination symlink owned by another uid while still following\n  the operator's own\n- CVE-2026-70452: fail closed when a hosts-deny token cannot be resolved, so a\n  transient DNS failure no longer admits a host the deny list names\n- CVE-2026-53783: inode-pin the rrsync-validated path and root the argument\n  handed to rsync at that pinned fd, refuse dangerous options in a restricted\n  directory, add the --drop-D option the restricted receiver needs, and keep\n  restricted-root paths working\n- CVE-2026-70460: pin the receiver option directories a peer can pivot through\n  rrsync",
